            "review_title": "Review at Tuan's Vietnamese Cuisine",
            "review_text": "Ania Z\nMoscow, Russia68 contributions\n0\nDelicious food against unsanitary conditions\nApr 2026 • Couples\nThe first place we went for lunch was Tuan’s Vietnamese Cuisine restaurant at 05 Trần Quang Khải, Lộc Thọ, Nha Trang. It was right next to our hotel, and since it was our first day of vacation, and we didn't really know where to go or where what was, it seemed like a great option. The restaurant has two floors, the first floor had all the tables taken, and we went up to the second floor, which is bigger, by the way. The place looks pretty simple, like a dining room. Service is quick, staff is polite. We ordered two smoothies, a seafood snack and a hot one. Everything is delicious and fresh, and the overall impression of the place was positive. Right up until the moment a cockroach ran across our table. To be honest, I, a squeamish man, felt like getting up and leaving immediately, and the undernourished food didn't seem so good anymore. The cockroach kept running out and hiding under the table, I finished some food, and we quickly left. The staff reacted calmly, by the way, as if nothing had happened. They offered to change the table, there were no compliments from the restaurant. A few days later, we met a couple on the street who also dined at the place and had a cockroach running around the table just like that. We never went back there again, even though the food was really good.\nRead more\nTranslated from Russian\nShow original\nWritten April 25, 2026",
